---
// What the App Store listing points at. Enough to solve the two things that go
// wrong, and a place to report the third.
const title = "Basaltty — Support";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Getting Basaltty working, and where to report a problem." />
    <link rel="icon" href="favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Syne:wght@400;600&family=Young+Serif&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <style>
      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 12vh 6vw 14vh;
        background: #04060a;
        color: #e2f4fb;
        font-family: Syne, ui-sans-serif, -apple-system, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.65;
      }
      main { max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 auto; }
      h1 { font-family: "Young Serif", Georgia, serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 2.4rem; margin: 0 0 0.4em; }
      h2 { font-family: "Young Serif", Georgia, serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 2.2em 0 0.4em; }
      p, li { color: rgba(226, 244, 251, 0.78); }
      a { color: #5fddf2; }
      .back { display: inline-block; margin-top: 3rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>Support</h1>

      <h2>What you need</h2>
      <p>
        Basaltty on your Mac, free from <a href=".">this site</a>, and Basaltty
        on your iPhone or iPad. Both devices signed into the same iCloud
        account, with iCloud Drive on.
      </p>

      <h2>The phone cannot find the Mac</h2>
      <p>
        Check that the Mac app is running, that both devices are on the same
        iCloud account, and that both are online — they do not have to be on the
        same network, but they do both have to reach iCloud.
      </p>

      <h2>The phone opens one Mac and not another</h2>
      <p>
        Without Basaltty Pro, your phone opens the Mac you chose in the Mac
        app's settings, under iPhone &amp; iPad. Pro opens all of them, and is
        bought in the app on iPhone or iPad.
      </p>

      <h2>Something else</h2>
      <p>
        Open an issue at
        <a href="https://github.com/FezVrasta/basaltty/issues">github.com/FezVrasta/basaltty</a>,
        with what you were doing and what happened. Replies are best effort, by
        one person.
      </p>

      <a class="back" href=".">Back to Basaltty</a>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
